# G33 independent stimulus audit

Read only this instruction and the assigned review input. Do not read generation judgments, research hypotheses, inference outputs, or any results directory. A/B labels conceal support/refute roles. You are an independent auditor. Every row includes claim, natural E_A/E_B, and experimental paraphrase X_A/X_B. Source sentences are not assumed to be valid merely because a dataset labeled them.

Independently judge each E and X sentence as `support`, `refute`, or `unclear` about the exact claim. Omission is not refutation; spelling variation is not a meaningful factual contrast; overlapping genre labels are not necessarily contradictory. Flag missing referents, ambiguous temporal scope, unsupported inference, serious corrupted source text. Check X_A/X_B preserve the decisive factual content of E_A/E_B WITHOUT adding new facts, asserted publication credentials or motivations, and are grammatical, reasonably natural, similarly styled and not exact copies. The X summaries are constructed stimuli, not source quotes or independently acquired facts.

Return EXACTLY one JSONL row per input to the assigned audit output: `id`, `e_a_relation`, `e_b_relation`, `x_a_relation`, `x_b_relation`, `source_valid` (boolean), `faithful` (boolean), `natural` (boolean), `accept` (boolean), `reason`. `accept` requires source validity, faithful/natural summaries, one support and one refute E, one support and one refute X, and E/X role alignment. Explain concrete item-specific findings, including reasons for passing, for every row. Reject rather than silently fix. Never drop a row. Write only the assigned output. Check JSON/count/ID completeness after writing.
